{% liquid
assign form_id = 'TextileInquiry-' | append: section.id
assign machine_names = 'LZ-1816L with standard conveyor table,LZ-1816L with optional automatic roll feeder' | split: ','
%}<div class="dd-textile"><section class="dd-textile__hero"><div class="dd-textile__wrap"><nav class="dd-textile__crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}#HomeIndustries">Industries</a><span>/</span><span>Textile &amp; Fabric Cutting</span></nav><div class="dd-textile__split"><div><p class="dd-textile__eyebrow">TEXTILES · PRINTED FABRICS · GARMENT PANELS</p><h1>Vision Laser Cutting for Printed Fabrics &amp; Textiles</h1><p class="dd-textile__lead">Plan fabric cutting around your printed designs, material and feeding needs. Explore panoramic vision contour cutting for garment panels, fabric graphics and decorative textile components.</p><div class="dd-textile__actions"><a class="dd-textile__button" href="#TextileContact">Get a Textile Cutting Solution</a><a href="#TextileSamples">Explore Cutting Applications →</a></div><p class="dd-textile__note">Free sample testing · Equipment configuration · Training &amp; technical support</p></div><figure>{{ images['textile-printed-contour-cutting.jpg'] | image_url: width: 1000 | image_tag: loading: 'eager', alt: 'Printed fabric shapes cut around their artwork on a conveyor table', fetchpriority: 'high' }}<figcaption>Printed fabric cutting demonstration. Printing and laser cutting are separate processes.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section>
<section class="dd-textile__section" id="TextileSamples"><div class="dd-textile__wrap"><p class="dd-textile__eyebrow">START WITH YOUR FINISHED COMPONENTS</p><h2>What textile products do you make?</h2><div class="dd-textile__grid"><article class="dd-textile__card">{{ images['lz-1816l-printed-garment-panels.jpg'] | image_url: width: 1000 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: 'Printed garment panels on the fabric laser conveyor table' }}<div class="dd-textile__body"><h3>Printed garment panels</h3><p>Contour cutting around suitable pre-printed apparel and sportswear designs. Review panel dimensions, print contrast and fabric stretch.</p></div></article><article class="dd-textile__card">{{ images['textile-printed-contour-cutting.jpg'] | image_url: width: 1000 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: 'Printed textile graphics with shaped cut outlines' }}<div class="dd-textile__body"><h3>Fabric graphics &amp; shaped pieces</h3><p>Cut printed textile artwork into the required outlines. Share the material composition and required border or cutting allowance.</p></div></article><article class="dd-textile__card">{{ images['lz-1816l-decorative-fabric-cutouts.jpg'] | image_url: width: 1000 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: 'Decorative floral cut-outs from the fabric laser application samples' }}<div class="dd-textile__body"><h3>Decorative cut-outs</h3><p>Evaluate perforations and decorative patterns for suitable textiles. Test narrow details and edge appearance on your own material.</p></div></article></div><p class="dd-textile__note">These are application samples, not customer production guarantees. Suitability depends on the exact fabric, coating, design and desired finish.</p></div></section>
<section class="dd-textile__section dd-textile__tint" id="TextileMachine"><div class="dd-textile__wrap dd-textile__split"><figure>{{ images['lz-1816l-panoramic-vision-cutout.png'] | image_url: width: 1000 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: 'LZ-1816L panoramic vision fabric laser cutter with standard conveyor table' }}<figcaption>Machine shown for reference. Computer and accessories are confirmed in the quotation.</figcaption></figure><div><p class="dd-textile__eyebrow">FEATURED TEXTILE CUTTING EQUIPMENT</p><h2>LZ-1816L Panoramic Vision Fabric Laser Cutter</h2><ul><li><strong>1800 × 1600 mm</strong> working area.</li><li><strong>150W × 2</strong> CO2 laser heads.</li><li>Dual-track asynchronous head configuration.</li><li>Panoramic vision positioning and conveyor feeding table as standard.</li><li>Separate automatic roll fabric feeder available as an option.</li></ul><a class="dd-textile__button" href="{{ routes.root_url }}products/lz-1816l-panoramic-vision-fabric-laser-cutting-machine">View LZ-1816L &amp; Get a Quote</a><p><a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/co2-laser">Browse CO2 Laser Cutting Machines →</a></p></div></div></section>
<section class="dd-textile__section"><div class="dd-textile__wrap"><h2>Choose the right fabric feeding setup</h2><div class="dd-textile__two"><div class="dd-textile__panel"><h3>Standard: conveyor feeding table</h3><p>The table moves fabric through the machine cutting area. It is included in the standard LZ-1816L configuration.</p></div><div class="dd-textile__panel"><h3>Optional: automatic roll fabric feeder</h3><p>A separate unit supplies roll fabric to the conveyor. Select it according to roll width, weight, diameter and material handling needs; it is not standard equipment.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="dd-textile__section dd-textile__tint"><div class="dd-textile__wrap dd-textile__split"><div><p class="dd-textile__eyebrow">FROM PRINTED ARTWORK TO CUT COMPONENTS</p><h2>Confirm the workflow with your actual fabric</h2><p>Printing, positioning, cutting and unloading each affect the finished panel. A sample test helps confirm the equipment and feeding setup before you place an order.</p><a class="dd-textile__button" href="#TextileContact">Request a Free Sample Test</a><p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AdQeEWKsP5k" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch the Fabric Cutting Demonstration →</a></p></div><ol class="dd-textile__steps"><li><h3>01 · Review material &amp; artwork</h3><p>Confirm composition, coating, usable width, print design and required cutting allowance.</p></li><li><h3>02 · Position and recognize the print</h3><p>Evaluate panoramic camera recognition with the actual layout, contrast and fabric condition.</p></li><li><h3>03 · Cut and inspect</h3><p>Review contour alignment, edge finish and small details on the test sample.</p></li><li><h3>04 · Confirm production configuration</h3><p>Agree the feeding option, accessories, training, quotation and order-specific delivery timing.</p></li></ol></div></section>
<section class="dd-textile__section"><div class="dd-textile__wrap dd-textile__split"><div><h2>Prepare your team for textile production</h2><p>We provide English manuals and videos, remote installation training, equipment-specific spare parts and technical support. On-site support can be arranged for the project.</p><p>Send fabric details, roll dimensions, artwork and your output target. Unknown coatings and blends require assessment; PVC-containing textiles are not suitable for this CO2 laser process.</p><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}#HomeFactory">Explore Our Factory &amp; Team →</a></div><div class="dd-textile__faq"><h2>Textile cutting questions</h2><details><summary>Is panoramic vision included on the LZ-1816L?</summary><p>Yes. Panoramic vision positioning is part of this model. The camera supports recognizing printed patterns for contour cutting. Your artwork, print contrast, fabric stretch and layout should be evaluated in a sample test.</p></details><details><summary>What is the difference between the conveyor table and automatic feeder?</summary><p>The conveyor feeding table is standard and moves fabric through the cutting area. The separate automatic roll fabric feeder is optional and supplies roll material to that table. The quotation states whether the optional feeder is included.</p></details><details><summary>Can the laser cut every fabric or coated textile?</summary><p>No. Confirm the exact composition, coating, thickness and required edge finish before testing. PVC-containing fabrics are not suitable for this CO2 laser process. Unknown blends and coatings need review.</p></details><details><summary>Does the machine print the fabric too?</summary><p>No. Textile printing is a separate process. The vision system helps cut around suitable pre-printed designs. Plain fabric jobs can also be evaluated using cutting files.</p></details><details><summary>What do you need for a free sample test?</summary><p>Send the fabric composition, sample or clear photos, artwork, usable width, panel dimensions and output target. For rolls, include diameter, weight and feeding requirements. Sample shipping arrangements are agreed separately.</p></details></div></div></section>
  <section class="dd-textile__section" id="TextileContact"><div class="dd-textile__wrap dd-textile__split"><div><p class="dd-textile__eyebrow">TELL US WHAT YOU WANT TO MAKE</p><h2>Get an equipment proposal for your textile production</h2><p>Share your fabric composition, roll width, printed artwork and production requirements. We will help you plan the equipment and a free sample test.</p><p><a href="mailto:info@gzcnc-laser.com">info@gzcnc-laser.com</a><br><a href="https://wa.me/8618988946615">WhatsApp: +86 189 8894 6615</a></p><p class="dd-textile__note">Need to share artwork or photos? Send them by email or WhatsApp. Name, email and message are required.</p></div>
    {% form 'contact', id: form_id %}
      <input type="hidden" name="contact[Source]" value="Textile and fabric cutting industry page">
      {% if form.posted_successfully? %}<div class="dd-textile__success" role="status" tabindex="-1" data-textile-success><strong>Thank you — your inquiry has been sent.</strong><p>Our team will review your requirements and contact you by email. You do not need to submit the same inquiry again.</p></div><dialog data-textile-dialog aria-labelledby="TextileSuccessTitle"><h2 id="TextileSuccessTitle">Inquiry sent successfully</h2><p>Thank you for contacting Dragon Diamond. Our team will review your requirements and contact you by email.</p><button type="button" class="dd-textile__button" data-textile-close>Got it</button></dialog>{% endif %}
      {% if form.errors %}<div role="alert">{{ form.errors | default_errors }}</div>{% endif %}
      <div class="dd-textile__fields"><div><label for="SignName-{{ section.id }}">Name *</label><input id="SignName-{{ section.id }}" name="contact[name]" autocomplete="name" value="{{ form.name | escape }}" required></div><div><label for="SignEmail-{{ section.id }}">Email *</label><input id="SignEmail-{{ section.id }}" name="contact[email]" type="email" autocomplete="email" value="{{ form.email | escape }}" required></div><div><label for="SignCompany-{{ section.id }}">Company</label><input id="SignCompany-{{ section.id }}" name="contact[Company]" autocomplete="organization" value="{{ form.Company | escape }}"></div><div><label for="SignWA-{{ section.id }}">WhatsApp</label><input id="SignWA-{{ section.id }}" name="contact[WhatsApp]" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" value="{{ form.WhatsApp | escape }}"></div></div>
      <label for="SignProduct-{{ section.id }}">Product Interested</label><select id="SignProduct-{{ section.id }}" name="contact[Product Interested]"><option>LZ-1816L / textile cutting advice</option>{% for name in machine_names %}<option>{{ name }}</option>{% endfor %}<option>Other textile cutting requirements</option></select>
      <label for="SignMessage-{{ section.id }}">Message *</label><textarea id="SignMessage-{{ section.id }}" name="contact[body]" rows="5" placeholder="Fabric composition, roll width, artwork, output target, feeder needs and destination..." required>{{ form.body | escape }}</textarea><button type="submit" class="dd-textile__button">Send Inquiry</button>
    {% endform %}
  </div></section></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":{{ request.origin | append: routes.root_url | json }}},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Textile & Fabric Cutting","item":{{ canonical_url | json }}}]}</script>{% stylesheet %}
.dd-textile{color:#163237;background:#fff;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.65}.dd-textile *{box-sizing:border-box}.dd-textile__wrap{max-width:1280px;margin:auto;padding:0 32px}.dd-textile__section{padding:76px 0}.dd-textile__tint{background:#eff5f4}.dd-textile__hero{background:#14373b;color:#fff;padding:135px 0 64px}.dd-textile__crumb{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:13px;margin-bottom:44px}.dd-textile .dd-textile__hero a{color:#80e0d7}.dd-textile__split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:48px;align-items:start}.dd-textile__hero .dd-textile__split{align-items:center}.dd-textile h1,.dd-textile h2,.dd-textile h3{font-family:var(--font-heading--family,Arial,sans-serif);color:inherit;letter-spacing:-.025em;line-height:1.16;margin:0 0 20px}.dd-textile h1{font-size:clamp(36px,3.4vw,54px)}.dd-textile h2{font-size:clamp(28px,2.6vw,38px)}.dd-textile h3{font-size:23px;margin-bottom:14px}.dd-textile p{margin:0 0 20px}.dd-textile__eyebrow{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;color:#087d83}.dd-textile__hero .dd-textile__eyebrow{color:#80e0d7}.dd-textile__lead{font-size:19px}.dd-textile__intro{max-width:800px}.dd-textile__actions{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:28px 0}.dd-textile a{color:#08777b;text-underline-offset:4px}.dd-textile__button{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:48px;padding:13px 20px;background:#087c80;color:#fff!important;border:0;border-radius:4px;font:700 15px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;text-decoration:none;cursor:pointer;text-align:center}.dd-textile__hero .dd-textile__button{background:#74dfd3;color:#10383b!important}.dd-textile figure{margin:0}.dd-textile img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.dd-textile__hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3;object-fit:cover;border-radius:10px}.dd-textile figcaption,.dd-textile__note{font-size:14px;margin-top:18px!important}.dd-textile__hero figcaption{color:#c4dcde}.dd-textile__grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:24px;margin-top:30px}.dd-textile__two{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:26px;margin-top:30px}.dd-textile__card{border:1px solid #d6e2e2;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column}.dd-textile__card img{aspect-ratio:16/10;object-fit:cover}.dd-textile__body{padding:24px;flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column}.dd-textile__body>a:last-child{margin-top:auto}.dd-textile__body ul{padding-left:20px;margin:0 0 24px;font-size:15px}.dd-textile__machine>a{background:#e8f0ef}.dd-textile__machine img{object-fit:contain;padding:18px;aspect-ratio:4/3}.dd-textile__panel{padding:26px;background:#fff;border-radius:8px;border-top:3px solid #087f82}.dd-textile__panel p{margin:0}.dd-textile__steps{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;border-left:2px solid #83c9c5}.dd-textile__steps li{padding:0 0 20px 26px}.dd-textile__steps li:last-child{padding-bottom:0}.dd-textile__steps h3{font-size:21px}.dd-textile__faq details{border-bottom:1px solid #b9cecc}.dd-textile__faq summary{padding:18px 0;min-height:48px;cursor:pointer;font-weight:700}.dd-textile__faq details p{padding:0 0 16px}.dd-textile__fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:0 18px}.dd-textile label{display:block;margin-bottom:6px;font-size:15px;font-weight:700}.dd-textile input,.dd-textile textarea,.dd-textile select{display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:48px;padding:12px;border:1px solid #a8c0c0;border-radius:4px;background:#fff;color:#163237;font:16px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:18px}.dd-textile textarea{resize:vertical}.dd-textile [id]{scroll-margin-top:125px}.dd-textile :focus-visible{outline:3px solid #d18b24;outline-offset:4px}.dd-textile__success{padding:20px;background:#e0f5ee;border:2px solid #087c80;margin-bottom:24px;border-radius:6px}.dd-textile dialog{max-width:520px;width:calc(100% - 32px);padding:30px;border:0;border-radius:10px;color:#163237}.dd-textile dialog::backdrop{background:#082429b3}.dd-textile__two img{object-fit:contain;background:#edf3f2}.dd-textile a{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:899px){.dd-textile__wrap{padding:0 22px}.dd-textile__split{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:32px}.dd-textile__grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.dd-textile__section{padding:48px 0}.dd-textile__hero{padding-top:105px}.dd-textile__crumb{margin-bottom:28px}.dd-textile__hero img{aspect-ratio:16/10}.dd-textile__machine img{max-height:310px}.dd-textile__two{grid-template-columns:1fr}.dd-textile__body{padding:22px}.dd-textile__actions{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}.dd-textile__fields{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
{% endstylesheet %}
{% javascript %}
function initTextileFeedback(){document.querySelectorAll('[data-textile-dialog]').forEach(dialog=>{if(dialog.dataset.ready)return;dialog.dataset.ready='true';const status=dialog.closest('form').querySelector('[data-textile-success]');dialog.querySelector('[data-textile-close]').addEventListener('click',()=>dialog.close());dialog.addEventListener('close',()=>status.focus());if(typeof dialog.showModal==='function')dialog.showModal();else status.focus();});}
initTextileFeedback();document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load',initTextileFeedback);
{% endjavascript %}
